  "releaseNotes": "memoize `ViewProjTrafo` per `(View, Proj)` like its sibling camera uniforms. It was the one camera uniform built as a fresh `AVal.map2` on every `TryGetUniform`, so every render object got a DISTINCT view-proj aval over the one camera — consumers that dedup global uniforms by aval identity (e.g. the heap arena) then saw N distinct sources and an O(N) fan-out per camera move. Now all render objects in a render control share ONE aval.\ndepend on `Aardvark.Rendering 5.7.0-prerelease0018` (heap: unified ref-counted-per-aval uniforms, real double-precision uniforms, camera composites derived from `View`/`Proj`).",
